    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="0732" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.416/7</note>
                <head>Representative Julius Kahn
                    to the Office of Foreign Trade Advisers
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">House of Representatives</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-02">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 2, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sirs</hi>: Confirming telephone conversation
                    had with your office this morning relative to the embargo placed on Australian
                    meats by the Australian government, would state that I received a telegram this
                    morning which reads as follows:</p>
                <p>Government of Australia has placed embargo upon shipments of Australian meats to
                    this country. This will work a hardship on Pacific Coast owing to fact immense
                    quantities handled here will seriously affect business interests in this
                        city.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d644-f1"/> Acting Secretary of State Robert Lansing has correspondence bearing on
                    this case. Use your best efforts to have Australian Government revoke this
                    order. All big packing houses and cold storage concerns on this coast deeply
                    interested. This merchandise is for Pacific Coast consumption only and
                    principally to fill United States Army and Navy contracts.</p>
                <p>I will greatly appreciate it if you will look into this matter and advise me
                    what, if anything, can be done in the premises.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Julius Kahn</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d644-f1" n="1" xml:id="d644-f1-content">
                <p>San Francisco.</p>
            </note>
